// The workspace that makes the split tree behave like one tree for everyday
// work: `go build ./...`, `go test ./...`, gopls and every editor resolve
// across module boundaries as they did before memql#3240.
//
// A go.work does NOT enforce the boundary, and must never be mistaken for it.
// Under workspace mode a module silently satisfies an import it does not
// `require` -- demonstrated on this tree in memql#3240 by giving the wire tier
// an upward import of component/safety:
//
//	$ go build ./...                 # workspace mode
//	exit=0                           # <- the violation is INVISIBLE
//
//	$ GOWORK=off go build ./...
//	violation_demo.go:7:8: no required module provides package
//	    github.com/znasllc-io/memql/component/safety
//	exit=1
//
// That is why the `module-boundaries` CI lane runs every module with
// GOWORK=off. The workspace is the ergonomics; the lane is the enforcement.
//
// Every module in the repository must be listed here, and the
// `module-boundaries` lane asserts that this list matches the go.mod files on
// disk. The point is that the two modes agree about what the tree IS: the lane
// verifies each module with GOWORK=off, while everything else -- the other CI
// lanes, gopls, `go test ./...` -- runs in workspace mode. A module missing
// from this list is verified by the lane but absent from the workspace, so the
// two are checking different trees and the difference is silent.

go 1.26.1

toolchain go1.26.5

use (
	.
	./component/actions
	./component/architecture
	./component/auth
	./component/bus
	./component/bus/gen
	./component/config
	./component/database
	./component/events
	./component/fileprocessor
	./component/genesis
	./component/grpc/gen
	./component/harness
	./component/healing
	./component/language
	./component/language/annotations
	./component/language/ast
	./component/language/dslclause
	./component/memql
	./component/metadata
	./component/metrics
	./component/node/gen
	./component/observe
	./component/planner
	./component/polyphon
	./component/provenance
	./component/safety
	./component/secret
	./core
	./docs
	./dsl
)
